<title>UK: SNOOKER-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP QUARTER-FINAL RESULT.</title>
<headline>SNOOKER-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP QUARTER-FINAL RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>SHEFFIELD, England 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result on Thursday of</p>
<p>the final quarter-final match (best of 25 frames) in the world</p>
<p>professional snooker championship, played late on Wednesday</p>
<p>(prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>12-James Wattana (Thailand) beat 4-John Parrott (England) 13-10</p>
<p>Frame scores (Wattana first): 4-129 72-48 41-72 99-0 65-11</p>
<p>82-1 15-58 94-3 7-76 70-17 0-88 9-75 94-6 0-129 81-1 101-15</p>
<p>62-77 83-15 32-66 73-17 59-69 68-50 79-64</p>
<p>Semifinal line up (May 1-3, best of 33 frames)</p>
<p>1-Stephen Hendry (Scotland) v Wattana</p>
<p>7-Ken Doherty (Ireland) v 14-Alain Robidoux (Canada)</p>
</text>
